{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --name-status a79a154df63cab2e827c3097df2e13b67989f501..565520e5c5ac23696ee8cf10bb9861c7052084c2 && git show 0af304d2983dc61c54079af5ac47531309c50459:attest/specs/217/spec.md | sed -n '1,260p' && sed -n '1,220p' attest/records/217/approval-01.json && sed -n '1,260p' tests/test_pass.py\"","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-hO8Ns8Uu' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-ICO6ZCH2' (errno=Operation not permitted)\nM\tattavo/cli.py\nM\tattavo/drive.py\nM\tattavo/report.py\nM\tattavo/verify.py\nA\tattest/records/217/approval-01.json\nA\tattest/records/217/build-01.started\nM\ttests/test_cli_help.py\nM\ttests/test_drive.py\nA\ttests/test_pass.py\nM\ttests/test_proof_five_elsewhere.py\nM\ttests/test_record_schemas.py\nM\ttests/test_report.py\nM\ttests/test_stub_ratio.py\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-qisohTcH' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-gMxoAh0J' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\n`attavo drive N` is a process that lasts as long as the stage it runs. It writes the invocation marker, pushes it, runs build or verify in-process, polls the forge for up to ten minutes, commits and pushes the record, and only then returns. Whoever called it holds it for the whole of that: the operator's shell, or the screen's server, which on #652 and #206 read six stage lines minutes late and on #194 twice lost a refusal nobody could read (#171). When the caller dies the stage dies with it, and the marker it pushed is what proof five later reads as a silence. `--recover` is a separate act a person must remember, and it refuses a tenant that has not declared a stall bound even when the invocation's pid is plainly gone. Two callers at once both run the stage: nothing holds an attempt.\n\nThis is R2 of the reconciler (`claude/reconciler-brief-2026-09-20.md`, rulings A, B, C's recovery half, F, G, H; 2026-09-20). `attavo drive N` becomes one pass: it reads the report (#206), acts at most once, and returns within seconds. The acts are three, one per report state that is the product's move: `owes-recovery` writes the died or hung record (what `--recover` did); `next-build` and `next-review` start the stage. Every other level is printed in the report's words and left, exit 0; exit 1 is a refusal. Starting a stage is the lease: the pass writes the marker, commits it, and pushes that commit as a plain fast-forward with no merge and no retry; a rejection that is not a fast-forward, or a ref another push holds, means another pass started this attempt, and the loser says so, resets its own marker commit, and starts nothing. A push the remote refuses outright is exit 1 and starts nothing. On a pushed marker the pass spawns `attavo worker N <stage> NN` in its own session, its stdout and stderr to `<git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.worker.log`, and returns; the worker outlives the pass, runs the stage in-process exactly as the drive did (counsel and file-stops on a non-pass record, one `git commit --only`, one push with the merge retry), and touches `<git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.heartbeat` every `ATTAVO_HEARTBEAT_S` seconds (15) while it runs. The report and the pass read alive from the heartbeat first (fresh within three beats: alive; stale: died) and fall back to the pid only when there is no heartbeat file. The stall bound decides hung, never died: with no `[drive].stall_after_s` a dead invocation is still recovered as died and an alive one is running for as long as it lives. A record written and not yet committed reads as running (the worker commits after it writes); one left uncommitted by a worker whose heartbeat is stale reads as a refusal naming the file. The review takes the checks the pass read on the head before the marker (ruling B): the pass writes them to `<git-dir>/attavo/verify-NN.forge-checks.json` and names the file in `ATTAVO_FORGE_CHECKS`; `attavo verify` reads that instead of polling, and polls as before when the variable is unset. The pass fast-forwards its working copy to origin's branch before reading, never while a worker holds the copy (a marker without its record, or a record not yet committed). `--again` starts the next attempt of a stopped stage, the operator's resume until rulings drive retries (R3, R4). `--all` runs one pass in every `../attavo-worktree-N` beside the checkout. `--until-ready` repeats the pass in one process, sleeping `ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S` between passes, until the level is the operator's or done (exit 0), a check concludes red (exit 1), or the checks have not concluded within `ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S` (exit 1). `--recover` is gone and exits 2 saying so. Nothing new is a record: the marker and the records are the worker's facts on the branch; the heartbeat, the worker log, and the forge-checks file are local under the git dir and never committed.\n\nThe stub under `stub/` is thin: a pass that reads the report, recovers, or writes and pushes the marker with the record push's own retry and starts the stage body in a child of its own session, with the review handed the checks; no heartbeat, no lease, no fast-forward, no `--again`, `--all`, or `--until-ready`. Seventeen of the tests named below fail on it. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the built tree with no `type: ignore`.\n\nRetires: the stage run inside `attavo drive`; the forge poll inside the drive (`_drive_step`); `--recover` as an operator's act; the refusal to recover without a stall bound; `attavo verify`'s own poll when a pass has read the checks; the synchronous `drive` calls in this repository's tests.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/drive.py\n- attavo/verify.py\n- attavo/report.py\n- attavo/cli.py\n- tests/test_pass.py\n- tests/test_drive.py\n- tests/test_report.py\n- tests/test_proof_five_elsewhere.py\n- tests/test_record_schemas.py\n- tests/test_stub_ratio.py\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- a-pass-returns-while-the-build-runs.sh: on a fixture tenant whose build adapter sleeps four seconds, attavo drive 1 exits 0 in under three seconds with the marker pushed and no build record yet, and the passing build record reaches origin within a minute\n- a-dead-invocation-is-recovered-by-a-pass.sh: on a fixture tenant carrying a pushed build-01.started whose pid is gone, attavo drive --recover 1 exits non-zero and writes nothing, and attavo drive 1 writes and pushes build-01.json with status failed and stop class died\n- the-review-reads-the-checks-the-pass-read.sh: on a fixture tenant whose checks command counts its calls, the pass that starts the review after a passed build reads the forge exactly once, on the head before its marker, and the passing verify record's forge_checks.sha is that head\n- the-tests-exist.sh: tests/test_pass.py carries the nine tests named, and tests/test_drive.py the ten\n{\n  \"sha\": \"a79a154df63cab2e827c3097df2e13b67989f501\",\n  \"spec_sha\": \"0af304d2983dc61c54079af5ac47531309c50459\",\n  \"approved_by\": \"dbean10\",\n  \"at\": \"2026-09-25T18:03:58Z\",\n  \"record_version\": 2,\n  \"item\": \"217\",\n  \"product_version\": \"v0.27.0\",\n  \"product_pin\": \"v0.27.0\"\n}\n\"\"\"The reconciler's R2 (claude/reconciler-brief-2026-09-20.md, rulings A, B,\nH): `attavo drive N` is one short pass that reads the report, acts at most\nonce, and returns; a stage runs in a detached worker with its own\nheartbeat; the marker's push is the lease; recovery is the pass's; the\nreview takes the checks the pass read on the pre-marker head.\n\nRun: python3 -m pytest tests -q\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport socket\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom helpers import commit_all, git, make_tenant\nfrom test_drive import (\n    GREEN_FORGE,\n    add_bare_remote,\n    add_drive_stall_bound,\n    add_forge,\n    approve_item,\n    head_of,\n    latest_record,\n    record_files,\n    records_dir,\n    remote_head,\n    run_attavo,\n    write_dead_marker,\n)\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nFAST = {\"ATTAVO_HEARTBEAT_S\": \"0.2\", \"ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_INTERVAL_S\": \"0.5\"}\n\n\ndef slow_adapter(root: Path, seconds: float) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A tenant-side build adapter: the product's own fixture adapter,\n    after `seconds` of sleep on the build stage.\"\"\"\n    d = root / \"attavo\" / \"adapters\" / \"fixture\"\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    run = d / \"run\"\n    run.write_text(f'#!/bin/sh\\nif [ \"${{ATTAVO_STAGE:-build}}\" = build ]; then sleep {seconds}; fi\\n'\n                   f'exec sh {ROOT / \"adapters\" / \"fixture\" / \"run\"}\\n')\n    run.chmod(0o755)\n    commit_all(root, \"a slow tenant-side adapter\")\n\n\ndef git_dir(root: Path) -> Path:\n    return Path(git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--absolute-git-dir\").strip())\n\n\ndef report(root: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", \"--report\", env=FAST)\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    out: dict[str, Any] = json.loads(run.stdout)\n    return out\n\n\ndef pushed(bare: Path, subject: str) -> bool:\n    log = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(bare), \"log\", \"--format=%s\", \"main\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n    return subject in log\n\n\ndef wait_for(pred: Any, seconds: float = 20) -> None:\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds\n    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\n        if pred():\n            return\n        time.sleep(0.2)\n    raise AssertionError(\"condition not met in time\")\n\n\ndef built_tenant(tmp_path: Path, seconds: float = 3) -> tuple[Path, Path]:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"build_valid\")\n    add_forge(root, GREEN_FORGE)\n    add_drive_stall_bound(root)\n    slow_adapter(root, seconds)\n    bare = add_bare_remote(root, tmp_path)\n    approve_item(root)\n    return root, bare\n\n\ndef test_a_pass_returns_while_the_worker_runs_and_the_worker_outlives_it(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root, bare = built_tenant(tmp_path, seconds=3)\n    started = time.monotonic()\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST)\n    elapsed = time.monotonic() - started\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    assert elapsed < 2.5, f\"the pass took {elapsed:.1f}s: it waited for the stage\"\n    assert \"Build started\" in run.stdout, run.stdout\n    assert (records_dir(root) / \"build-01.started\").exists()\n    assert remote_head(bare, \"main\") == head_of(root), \"the marker was not pushed before the pass returned\"\n    assert record_files(root, \"build\") == [], \"the record existed before the worker could have written it\"\n    wait_for(lambda: record_files(root, \"build\") != [])\n    wait_for(lambda: remote_head(bare, \"main\") == head_of(root))\n    assert latest_record(root, \"build\")[\"status\"] == \"pass\"\n\n\ndef test_the_worker_touches_its_heartbeat_and_the_report_reads_running_by_it(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root, _ = built_tenant(tmp_path, seconds=3)\n    assert run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST).returncode == 0\n    beat = git_dir(root) / \"attavo\" / \"build-01.heartbeat\"\n    wait_for(beat.exists, 5)\n    first = beat.stat().st_mtime\n    time.sleep(0.6)\n    assert beat.stat().st_mtime > first, \"the heartbeat did not move\"\n    r = report(root)\n    assert (r[\"state\"], r[\"kind\"]) == (\"running\", \"waits\"), r\n    wait_for(lambda: record_files(root, \"build\") != [])\n\n\ndef test_a_stale_heartbeat_reads_died_though_the_pid_lives_and_a_fresh_one_reads_alive(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"build_valid\")\n    add_forge(root, GREEN_FORGE)\n    add_drive_stall_bound(root, 600)\n    approve_item(root)\n    d = records_dir(root)\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    marker = d / \"build-01.started\"\n    now = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime())\n    marker.write_text(json.dumps({\"at\": now, \"host\": socket.gethostname(),\n                                  \"pid\": os.getpid(), \"sha\": head_of(root), \"product_version\": \"fixture\"}))\n    commit_all(root, \"a marker whose pid is this test\")\n    beat = git_dir(root) / \"attavo\" / \"build-01.heartbeat\"\n    beat.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    beat.touch()\n    os.utime(beat, (time.time() - 60, time.time() - 60))\n    r = report(root)\n    assert (r[\"state\"], r[\"stop_class\"]) == (\"owes-recovery\", \"died\"), r\n    beat.touch()\n    r = report(root)\n    assert r[\"state\"] == \"running\", r\n\n\ndef test_two_passes_at_once_start_one_worker_and_the_loser_says_so(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root, bare = built_tenant(tmp_path, seconds=3)\n    commit_all(root, \"the approval, so a second checkout carries it\")\n    git(root, \"push\", \"-q\", \"origin\", \"HEAD:main\")\n    clone = tmp_path / \"second\"\n    git(root.parent, \"clone\", \"-q\", \"-b\", git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\").strip(), str(bare), str(clone))\n    git(clone, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"test@example.com\")\n    git(clone, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"Attavo Test\")\n    git(clone, \"remote\", \"set-head\", \"origin\", \"-a\")\n    env = dict(os.environ)\n    env.update(FAST)\n    procs = [subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, str(ROOT / \"bin\" / \"attavo\"), \"drive\", \"1\"], cwd=str(c),\n                              env=env, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)\n             for c in (root, clone)]\n    outs = [p.communicate(timeout=30)[0] for p in procs]\n    started = [o for o in outs if \"Build started\" in o]\n    held = [o for o in outs if \"another pass holds\" in o]\n    assert len(started) == 1 and len(held) == 1, outs\n    log = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(bare), \"log\", \"--format=%s\", \"main\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n    assert log.count(\"build invocation 01 started\") == 1, log\n    wait_for(lambda: \"build record for item 1\" in subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(bare), \"log\", \"--format=%s\", \"main\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout)\n\n\ndef test_a_pass_recovers_a_dead_invocation_and_recover_is_gone(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"build_valid\")\n    add_forge(root, GREEN_FORGE)\n    add_drive_stall_bound(root)\n    approve_item(root)\n    write_dead_marker(root, \"build\", 1)\n    gone = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"--recover\", \"1\", env=FAST)\n    assert gone.returncode == 2 and \"gone\" in gone.stderr, gone.stdout + gone.stderr\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST)\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    rec = latest_record(root, \"build\")\n    assert rec[\"stop\"][\"class\"] == \"died\", rec[\"stop\"]\n\n\ndef test_the_review_takes_the_checks_the_pass_read_and_never_polls(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"build_valid\")\n    calls = tmp_path / \"forge-calls.txt\"\n    forge = tmp_path / \"forge.sh\"\n    forge.write_text(f'#!/bin/sh\\necho \"$1\" >> {calls}\\nprintf \"ci success\\\\n\"\\n')\n    forge.chmod(0o755)\n    add_forge(root, f\"sh {forge}\")\n    add_drive_stall_bound(root)\n    slow_adapter(root, 0)\n    bare = add_bare_remote(root, tmp_path)\n    approve_item(root)\n    assert run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST).returncode == 0\n    wait_for(lambda: pushed(bare, \"build record for item 1\"))\n    calls.write_text(\"\")\n    pre_marker = head_of(root)\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST)\n    assert \"Review started\" in run.stdout, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    wait_for(lambda: record_files(root, \"verify\") != [])\n    rec = latest_record(root, \"verify\")\n    assert rec[\"status\"] == \"pass\", rec\n    assert rec[\"forge_checks\"][\"sha\"] == pre_marker, (rec[\"forge_checks\"], pre_marker)\n    read_by = [l for l in calls.read_text().split() if l]\n    assert read_by == [pre_marker], f\"the forge was read {len(read_by)} time(s) after the build: {read_by}\"\n\n\ndef test_until_ready_is_a_loop_of_passes_that_returns_at_ready(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root, _ = built_tenant(tmp_path, seconds=0)\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", \"--until-ready\", env=FAST)\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    assert \"Build started\" in run.stdout and \"Review started\" in run.stdout, run.stdout\n    assert run.stdout.strip().endswith(\"Ready to merge\"), run.stdout\n    assert report(root)[\"state\"] == \"ready-to-merge\"\n\n\ndef test_a_stopped_stage_is_left_alone_by_a_pass_and_started_again_by_again(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"build_valid\")\n    add_forge(root, GREEN_FORGE)\n    add_drive_stall_bound(root)\n    approve_item(root)\n    write_dead_marker(root, \"build\", 1)\n    assert run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST).returncode == 0\n    assert latest_record(root, \"build\")[\"stop\"][\"class\"] == \"died\"\n    plain = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", env=FAST)\n    assert plain.returncode == 0 and \"Needs you\" in plain.stdout, plain.stdout\n    assert not (records_dir(root) / \"build-02.started\").exists()\n    again = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"1\", \"--again\", env=FAST)\n    assert \"Build started\" in again.stdout, again.stdout + again.stderr\n    assert (records_dir(root) / \"build-02.started\").exists()\n    wait_for(lambda: len(record_files(root, \"build\")) == 2)\n\n\ndef test_all_runs_one_pass_in_every_working_copy_beside_the_checkout(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"build_valid\", name=\"tenant\")\n    add_forge(root, GREEN_FORGE)\n    add_drive_stall_bound(root)\n    slow_adapter(root, 0)\n    bare = add_bare_remote(root, tmp_path)\n    for n in (\"1\",):\n        copy = tmp_path / f\"attavo-worktree-{n}\"\n        git(root, \"worktree\", \"add\", \"-q\", \"-b\", f\"attavo/{n}-x\", str(copy), \"HEAD\")\n        git(copy, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"test@example.com\")\n        git(copy, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"Attavo Test\")\n        approve_item(copy, n)\n    run = run_attavo(root, \"drive\", \"--all\", env=FAST)\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stdout + run.stderr\n    assert \"attavo-worktree-1: attavo drive: Build started\" in run.stdout, run.stdout\n    wait_for(lambda: record_files(tmp_path / \"attavo-worktree-1\", \"build\") != [])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
