shed marker authorizes a worker to start.", "rejection_test": "test_drive_without_an_origin_refuses_and_starts_no_worker", "severity": "Blocking when the checkout has no `origin`: the marker is committed locally and a worker starts even though no marker was pushed, so another checkout has no lease fact preventing the same attempt from running."}, {"title": "Pre-pass synchronization rebases local commits instead of only fast-forwarding", "specimen": "attavo/drive.py:315", "retires": "Closes divergence from the approved requirement that a pass fast-forward its working copy to the origin branch before reading.", "rejection_test": "test_drive_refuses_or_leaves_the_checkout_unchanged_when_origin_cannot_be_fast_forwarded", "severity": "Blocking when both the local branch and origin have advanced: the pass rewrites local commits with `git rebase FETCH_HEAD`, changing operator-authored commit identities before taking its lease."}, {"title": "The worker entry point does not require the lease marker it claims to execute", "specimen": "attavo/drive.py:431", "retires": "Closes the bypass around the marker-push lease by requiring a worker invocation to correspond to an existing committed marker for the same stage and attempt.", "rejection_test": "test_worker_refuses_without_a_matching_committed_invocation_marker", "severity": "Blocking when `attavo worker N <stage> NN` is invoked directly or with a mismatched attempt: it runs the stage without proving that this process owns a pushed marker, permitting duplicate or unleased execution."}], "tests_named": ["test_losing_a_marker_push_preserves_unrelated_tracked_and_untracked_working_tree_changes", "test_report_reads_an_uncommitted_passing_build_or_verify_as_running_then_refused_when_its_heartbeat_stales", "test_a_pass_recovers_a_dead_verify_invocation_with_the_current_build_binding", "test_drive_without_an_origin_refuses_and_starts_no_worker", "test_drive_refuses_or_leaves_the_checkout_unchanged_when_origin_cannot_be_fast_forwarded", "test_worker_refuses_without_a_matching_committed_invocation_marker"]}